sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant FDA as FDA / regulator
  participant RC as Recall coordinator
  participant SUP as Supplier
  participant OPS as DC / store
  participant FSM as Food-safety manager
  participant CON as Consumers

  FDA->>RC: Public notice / enforcement record
  Note over FDA,RC: Official scope evidence — retailer response starts here
  opt Public communication is applicable
    FDA-->>CON: Official recall information
    Note over FDA,CON: FDA or the recalling firm may issue a public warning under the real strategy
  end
  RC->>RC: Verify product, code, plant, date, geography, hazard
  RC->>SUP: Request lot and shipment evidence
  SUP-->>RC: Lot/source documents or an explicit evidence gap
  RC->>OPS: Trace receipt, transfers, inventory, sales, returns
  OPS-->>RC: Event IDs, quantities, facilities, acknowledgements
  RC->>FSM: Review predicate, matches, equation, gaps, proposed containment

  alt Ambiguity, unaccounted units, or missing acknowledgement
    FSM-->>RC: Edit, reject, or escalate
    Note over RC,FSM: Internal closure blocked
  else Evidence gates pass
    FSM-->>RC: Authorize exact simulated action and separate closure review
    RC->>OPS: Record simulated action and monitor facility response
    OPS-->>RC: Receipt, disposition evidence, acknowledgement
  end

  Note over FDA,CON: RecallOps contacts neither regulators nor consumers
  Note over FDA,FSM: FDA termination is separate from retailer internal closure
